From f9a742e7670451f64bccc207a60b092071f037a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:05:53 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: derive the first conv's pad value instead of
 hardcoding it

A padded tap has to contribute nothing, which means reading as the input zero
point. The CMAC sees the input with 0x80 subtracted, so the byte to write is
in_zp - 0x80, replicated across the three input lanes. 0x00808080 is that byte
for an input whose zero point is 0, a plain image tensor, which is what the
capture this function came from used. MobileNet's conv0 has zero point 128 and
wants 0x00000000.

The generic path already carries this fix and its comment records the symptom:
the output border ring is wrong and everything inside it is right. conv0 shows
exactly that. Its impulse decodes to the right plane and tap at correlation
1.000 on a 32x32 interior crop while an affine fit over the whole 112x112
surface reaches only 0.89.

Third literal in fill_regcmd_firstconv found wrong this way, after the padding
amounts and the coefficient region collision. All three were correct for the
single model the function was written from.

ROCKET_FC_PAD_VAL forces a value and 0x00808080 restores the literal.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
index 9def453..317c609 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
@@ -181,7 +181,30 @@ fill_first_regcmd_rk3576_firstconv(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
    R_CNA(0x1080, rkt_env_u32("ROCKET_FC_PAD",
                              (task->pad_right << 24) | (task->pad_bottom << 16) |
                              (task->pad_left << 8) | task->pad_top));
-   R_CNA(0x1084, 0x00808080);
+   /*
+    * The PAD VALUE, derived rather than hardcoded, for the same reason 0x1080
+    * above is.
+    *
+    * A padded tap must contribute nothing, which means it has to read as the
+    * input zero point. The CMAC sees the input with 0x80 subtracted, so the
+    * byte to write is in_zp - 0x80, replicated across the three input lanes.
+    * 0x00808080 is that byte for an input whose zero point is 0, which is what
+    * a plain image tensor has and what the capture this function came from
+    * used. MobileNet's conv0 has zero point 128 and wants 0x00000000.
+    *
+    * The generic path already carries this fix, and its comment records the
+    * symptom: the output border ring is wrong, everything inside it is right.
+    * That is exactly what conv0 shows. Its impulse decodes to the right plane
+    * and tap at correlation 1.000 on a 32x32 interior crop, while an affine
+    * fit over the whole 112x112 surface only reaches 0.89.
+    *
+    * ROCKET_FC_PAD_VAL forces a value, and 0x00808080 restores the literal.
+    */
+   {
+      uint32_t pv = (uint32_t)(((int32_t)task->input_zero_point - 0x80) & 0xff);
+      R_CNA(0x1084, rkt_env_u32("ROCKET_FC_PAD_VAL",
+                                (pv << 16) | (pv << 8) | pv));
+   }
    R_CNA(0x1088, feature_addr); /* input feature base addr */
    R_CNA(0x108c, 0x000f000f);
    R_CNA(0x1090, 0x0000002a);   /* CBUF input line-stride = ceil(224/16)*3 */
-- 
